2025-05-01 00:58:58 - Thread-155 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage for the requested report  

• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  – "content": holds the full text of every sampled file –‑ this is the column that must be split into individual lines and tested for the three categories (trailing / Space / Other).  
  – "id": can be used to keep each file distinct while exploding lines.  
  – "sample_repo_name": allows filtering to a specific repository, or aggregating by repository if needed.  
  – "sample_path": can be used to see which file a line belongs to.  

• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES (optional)  
  – "id": link‐key to “SAMPLE_CONTENTS"."id" when metadata about the file (mode, ref, …) is required.  

Typical conditions that might be useful  
1. WHERE "sample_repo_name" = '<exact‑repo>'                       – work on a single repository.  
2. WHERE "content" IS NOT NULL                                     – ignore files without stored content.  
3. REGEXP_LIKE(line_txt, '\\s$')                                   – line ends with a blank character  (“trailing”).  
4. REGEXP_LIKE(line_txt, '^ ')                                     – line starts with a space (“Space”).  
5. NOT (…)                                                         – everything else (“Other”).  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each capped with LIMIT 20) that progress from simple inspection to the logic needed for the final report.  Replace <repo‑name‑here> when you want to focus on one repository.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at a few raw files and their sizes.
SELECT 
    "sample_repo_name",
    "sample_path",
    "size"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "content" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show one file’s full content (truncated here) to understand the line structure.
SELECT
    "sample_repo_name",
    "sample_path",
    LEFT("content", 2000) AS "content_first_2k"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_repo_name" = '<repo-name-here>'
  AND "content" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Use SPLIT_TO_TABLE to explode one file into separate rows per line.
SELECT
    c."sample_repo_name",
    c."sample_path",
    line.value::STRING AS "line_txt",
    line.index AS "line_no"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
WHERE c."sample_repo_name" = '<repo-name-here>'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Detect lines that end with a blank character (trailing spaces / tabs).
SELECT 
    c."sample_repo_name",
    c."sample_path",
    line.value::STRING AS "line_txt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
WHERE REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '\\s$')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Detect lines that start with an actual space (leading blank).
SELECT 
    c."sample_repo_name",
    c."sample_path",
    line.value::STRING AS "line_txt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
WHERE REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '^ ')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Categorise every line of one repository into Trailing / Space / Other.
SELECT
    CASE
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '\\s$')        THEN 'Trailing'
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '^ ')          THEN 'Space'
         ELSE 'Other'
    END                       AS "line_type",
    COUNT(*)                  AS "lines"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
WHERE c."sample_repo_name" = '<repo-name-here>'
GROUP BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Same as #6 but across ALL repositories, still limited for test.
SELECT
    CASE
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '\\s$')        THEN 'Trailing'
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '^ ')          THEN 'Space'
         ELSE 'Other'
    END                       AS "line_type",
    COUNT(*)                  AS "lines"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 2 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Break down the counts by repository as well.
SELECT
    c."sample_repo_name",
    CASE
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '\\s$')        THEN 'Trailing'
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '^ ')          THEN 'Space'
         ELSE 'Other'
    END                       AS "line_type",
    COUNT(*)                  AS "lines"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
GROUP BY 1, 2
ORDER BY 1, 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Join with SAMPLE_FILES to also output the git "id" and file mode.
SELECT
    f."repo_name",
    f."path",
    f."mode",
    CASE
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '\\s$')        THEN 'Trailing'
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '^ ')          THEN 'Space'
         ELSE 'Other'
    END                       AS "line_type"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  f
JOIN GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c
      ON f."id" = c."id"
     AND f."repo_name" = c."sample_repo_name",
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
WHERE f."repo_name" = '<repo-name-here>'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final production‑style query: global counts for Trailing / Space / Other (no LIMIT in real run; kept here).
SELECT
    CASE
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '\\s$')        THEN 'Trailing'
         WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '^ ')          THEN 'Space'
         ELSE 'Other'
    END                       AS "line_type",
    COUNT(*)                  AS "total_occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 2 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
