```sql
--Description / Thinking process:
-- Objective:  Count how many lines across ALL stored files fall into
--   • Trailing  – ends with at least one space or tab before the newline
--   • Space     – starts with a single space (could be followed by anything)
--   • Other     – everything else
--
-- Steps encoded below:
-- 1. Work from SAMPLE_CONTENTS because it stores raw file text in column "content".
-- 2. Use LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(…, '\n') to explode each file’s text into individual
--    line rows (Snowflake keeps both the line text and its index).
-- 3. In the SELECT list, build a CASE expression:
--        REGEXP_LIKE(line, '[ \t]+$')     → 'Trailing'
--        REGEXP_LIKE(line, '^ ')          → 'Space'
--        else                              'Other'
-- 4. Aggregate with COUNT(*) per category and order for readability.
-- 5. Filter out rows where "content" is NULL so we only process files we have.
-- The result gives the total occurrences for each category across the entire sample.
SELECT
    CASE
        WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '[ \t]+$') THEN 'Trailing'
        WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(line.value::STRING, '^ ')      THEN 'Space'
        ELSE 'Other'
    END                               AS "line_type",
    COUNT(*)                          AS "total_occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') line
WHERE c."content" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 2 DESC;
```
